Vacuity/disjunct read (all 16 declarations, including private helpers): none has a conclusion disjunction, including within the existential meanings. There is no alternative conclusion that typing, an empty instance, or an assumed comparison success can satisfy while abandoning equality.
- eqData_apply: composes actual evaluations of x, y and the body into evaluation of the generated application. It assumes the three component derivations, not the application conclusion. A composition lemma, not a claim of unconditional termination.
- data_get: turns environment and first-field lookup facts into a deployed BigStep field-selection derivation; no assumed evaluation conclusion.
- conform_find: produces a value that actually occurs at the selected label and conforms to its selected type. The existential is pinned by lookup; it cannot choose an unrelated datum.
- canon_find: canonical membership implies actual first-match lookup. Ascending rows exclude a shadowing duplicate; membership alone is insufficient on arbitrary rows.
- conform_ext: equal lookups imply equality of the complete, same-shaped, canonically labelled data rows. It does not assume row equality; ascending plus RowConforms prevents hidden tails.
- find_map: selected values survive the label-preserving map; no unconstrained witness or vacuous alternative.
- find_mem: successful first-match lookup yields actual pair membership; lookup is not defined as membership.
- fields_meaning: the premise supplies semantics for each individual selected field; the conclusion constructs execution of the generated conjunction and relates its result to all selected fields. The empty-row base is appropriately true, but nonempty rows remain constrained. It does not assume execution of the conjunction.
- eqDataBody_meaning: constructs a Boolean AND its BigStep execution AND equality equivalence for arbitrary conforming d/e at canonical T. Neither equal-only nor result-exists premises are present. The function branch has no Conforms inhabitant, as documented; this does not empty the nat/bool/bytes/digest/record/sum cases. Equal and unequal naturals are both conforming instances.
- eqData_true: hx and hy bind dx/dy to the very x/y passed to eqData; h binds b to evaluation of that exact comparison. Determinism connects h to the execution constructed by eqDataBody_meaning. The conclusion is equality of those actual input data, not of freely chosen shadow terms. h is not being used to assume equality. Both directions are substantive.
- eqData_nested_checks: the deployed infer checks the generated nested comparison as Bool.
- eqData_nested_equal: the deployed bounded run returns true for the equal nested fixture.
- eqData_nested_payload_diff: the same-tag, unequal payload fixture returns false; real mutation evidence below.
- eqData_nested_tag_diff: equal payloads with different tags return false, exercising the separate sum-label decision.
- eqData_bool_diff: true versus false returns false through the generated Boolean code.
- eqData_empty_record: empty records compare true; a concrete base-case regression tooth, not a claim that bounds arbitrary instances.

Meaning boundary: hx/hy require operand values to be literally Data.toVal values. This is appropriate for reified World data and does connect actual operands, but it is not a theorem about arbitrary lazy record closures merely having the same extracted data. Nor does the BigStep existence theorem supply a bounded-fuel run guarantee. The fixture teeth separately run the deployed machine with fuel 1000 and Bounds.stackMax. None of these stronger claims should be attributed to eqData_true.

